## Summary of Logic Flow

### Example: Single Threshold (Success Case)

```
CLI: frai eval --outputs outputs.json --threshold exact_match=0.9
  ↓
runEvalCommand(options: { outputs: 'outputs.json', threshold: ['exact_match=0.9'] })
  ↓
parseThresholds(['exact_match=0.9'])
  → Validates format: ✓
  → Validates range (0.9 is between 0-1): ✓
  → Returns: { thresholds: { exact_match: 0.9 }, errors: [] }
  ↓
Load dataset and run evaluations
  → evaluations = [
      { id: 'exact_match', score: 0.95 },
      { id: 'toxicity', score: 1.0 },
      { id: 'length_variance', score: 0.85 }
    ]
  ↓
validateThresholds({ exact_match: 0.9 }, evaluations)
  → Metric 'exact_match' exists: ✓
  → Returns: errors = []
  ↓
generateReport(..., { exact_match: 0.9 })
  → evaluateThresholds({ exact_match: 0.9 }, evaluations)
    → score (0.95) >= min (0.9): ✓ passed
  → report.passed = true
  → report.thresholds = [
      { metric: 'exact_match', min: 0.9, score: 0.95, passed: true }
    ]
  ↓
writeReport(report, 'json')
  → report.json written with passed: true, thresholds: [...]
  ↓
log.success('Evaluation report generated.')
  ↓
thresholds exist && report.passed: exit with 0
  ✓ Exit 0 (success)
```

### Example: Malformed Threshold

```
CLI: frai eval --outputs outputs.json --threshold exact_match
  ↓
runEvalCommand(options: { outputs: 'outputs.json', threshold: ['exact_match'] })
  ↓
parseThresholds(['exact_match'])
  → Validates format: ✗ doesn't match /^([a-z_]+)=(.+)$/
  → errors = ["Invalid threshold format 'exact_match'. Expected format: <metric>=<number>"]
  ↓
thresholdErrors.length > 0: log error and exit
  log.error("Invalid threshold format 'exact_match'. Expected format: <metric>=<number>")
  ✗ Exit 2 (usage error)
  → Report not written
```

### Example: Threshold Fails

```
CLI: frai eval --outputs outputs.json --threshold exact_match=0.99
  ↓
runEvalCommand(options: { threshold: ['exact_match=0.99'] })
  ↓
parseThresholds(['exact_match=0.99']): ✓
  → { thresholds: { exact_match: 0.99 }, errors: [] }
  ↓
validateThresholds({ exact_match: 0.99 }, evaluations): ✓
  → Metric exists, format valid, range valid
  ↓
generateReport(..., { exact_match: 0.99 })
  → score (0.95) >= min (0.99): ✗ failed
  → report.passed = false
  → report.thresholds = [
      { metric: 'exact_match', min: 0.99, score: 0.95, passed: false }
    ]
  ↓
writeReport(report, 'json')
  ✓ Report written with passed: false
  ↓
thresholds exist && !report.passed: exit with 1
  ✗ Exit 1 (evaluation failure)
```

---

## Exit Code Summary

| Scenario | Code | When |
|----------|------|------|
| No errors, all thresholds pass | 0 | Successful evaluation |
| No errors, no thresholds specified | 0 | Normal completion |
| Threshold format error | 2 | parseThresholds catches malformed format |
| Threshold range error | 2 | parseThresholds catches out-of-range value |
| Unknown metric in threshold | 2 | validateThresholds catches unknown metric |
| Threshold failed (score < min) | 1 | evaluateThresholds returns passed: false |
| Metric score is null | 1 | Null score can't meet threshold, passed: false |

